    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the owner's date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting **1 July**, labelled by the calendar year in which it ends, e.g. Aug 2026 \u2192 FY27).\n\n**`OwnerDerivations.java`** (`model/`):\n- Added `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` \u2014 the fiscal year (as a 4-digit year) containing a date: Jul\u2013Dec \u2192 year+1, Jan\u2013Jun \u2192 year.\n- Added `fiscalYear(LocalDate)` \u2014 returns `FY<YY>` (last two digits of the fiscal year), or `null` when no registration date.\n- Added `elapsedFiscalYears(registrationDate, asOf)` and rewrote the shared `tenureExceedsYear` test to fire once **at least one whole fiscal year has elapsed** (crossed a 1 July boundary), replacing the old 365-day window.\n- Changed `membershipNumber` so its `-M<YY>` segment uses the **fiscal year's** last two digits rather than the raw registration-date year.\n- Swapped the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import for `java.time.Month`.\n\n**`Owner.java`**: added the `@Transient getFiscalYear()` derived getter delegating to `OwnerDerivations.fiscalYear(registrationDate)`. Since the stored `registrationDate` is already business-day-adjusted by the controller (`rollToBusinessDay`, line 274), the fiscal year is correctly derived from the adjusted date.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: added a `fiscalYear` (`FY<YY>`, read-only) property to the `Owner` schema \u2014 MapStruct auto-maps `getFiscalYear()` into the generated DTO/JSON \u2014 and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nThe acceptance suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), and the audit log confirms the behaviour change: a `2026-09-07` registration now yields `membershipNumber=\u2026-M27` and `fiscalYear=FY27`.",
